      "message": "You\u0027re right. In nghttp2 v1.69.0, the DATA callback path ignores -521: it only handles NGHTTP2_ERR_PAUSE or fatal values below -900. The earlier runtime run established that memory stopped growing, not that nghttp2 tore down the connection; that sentence overclaimed the evidence.\n\nPS3 explicitly submits RST_STREAM(ENHANCE_YOUR_CALM), returns 0 from the callback, releases the partial request body, and prevents request dispatch. The new tests verify the RST frame, body release, and handler suppression for both an accumulated and a declared oversized body, plus a subsequent request on the same nghttp2 session. A runtime probe also verifies that a new stream receives a response over the same connection after the reset. I shortened the subject and wrapped the commit body.",
